  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n1. Pod `orders-api-7b7dfdc66d-s2556` in namespace `demo-apps` logs `WARN database orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432 not reachable ([Errno -2] Name or service not known), retrying` (pod log).\n2. The pod fails its readiness check with `Readiness probe failed: HTTP probe failed with statuscode: 503` (Kubernetes event).\n3. ConfigMap `orders-config` sets `DB_HOST` to `orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432`, but only Service `orders-db` exists in namespace `demo-apps` (ConfigMap and Service definitions).\n\n### Ruled-out leads\n1. Resource exhaustion is ruled out because the pod consumes only 14Mi memory out of its 256Mi limit and 1m CPU (pod metrics).\n2. Node-level issues are ruled out because adjacent pods on node `k3d-spike-001-agent-0` remain healthy and ready (pod status).\n\n### Root cause\nDeployment change CI-2459 updated `orders-config` to use non-existent database host `orders-db-primary.demo-apps.svc:5432`, causing database connectivity checks to fail during readiness probing.\n\n### Recommended action\nThe orders team should revert `DB_HOST` in ConfigMap `orders-config` to `orders-db.demo-apps.svc:5432` and restart the deployment.",
